{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSound","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tempo is expressed in quarter notes per minute. If 0, the sound-generating program should prompt the user at"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the time of compiling a sound (MIDI) file.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dynamics (or MIDI velocity) are expressed as a percentage of the default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dacapo indicates to go back to the beginning of the movement. When used it always has the value “yes”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Segno and dalsegno are used for backwards jumps to a segno sign; coda and tocoda are used for forward jumps to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a coda sign. If there are multiple jumps, the value of these parameters can be used to name and distinguish","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them. If segno or coda is used, the divisions attribute can also be used to indicate the number of divisions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per quarter note. Otherwise sound and MIDI generating programs may have to recompute this.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, a dalsegno or dacapo attribute indicates that the jump should occur the first time through, while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"a tocoda attribute indicates the jump should occur the second time through. The time that jumps occur can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed by using the time-only attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The forward-repeat attribute indicates that a forward repeat sign is implied but not displayed. It is used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example in two-part forms with repeats, such as a minuet and trio where no repeat is displayed at the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the trio. This usually occurs after a barline. When used it always has the value of “yes”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fine attribute follows the final note or rest in a movement with a da capo or dal segno direction. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numeric, the value represents the actual duration of the final note or rest, which can be ambiguous in written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation and different among parts and voices. The value may also be “yes” to indicate no change to the final"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the sound element applies only particular times through a repeat, the time-only attribute indicates which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times to apply the sound element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pizzicato in a sound element effects all following notes. Yes indicates pizzicato, no indicates arco."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pan and elevation attributes are deprecated in Version 2.0. The pan and elevation elements in the midi-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instrument element should be used instead. The meaning of the pan and elevation attributes is the same as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pan and elevation elements. If both are present, the mid-instrument elements take priority."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The damper-pedal, soft-pedal, and sostenuto-pedal attributes effect playback of the three common piano pedals"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their MIDI controller equivalents. The yes value indicates the pedal is depressed; no indicates the pedal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is released. A numeric value from 0 to 100 may also be used for half pedaling. This value is the percentage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the pedal is depressed. A value of 0 is equivalent to no, and a value of 100 is equivalent to yes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instrument changes, MIDI devices, MIDI instruments, and playback techniques are changed using the instrument-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change, midi-device, midi-instrument, and play elements. When there are multiple instances of these elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they should be grouped together by instrument using the id attribute values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The offset element is used to indicate that the sound takes place offset from the current score position. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sound element is a child of a direction element, the sound offset element overrides the direction offset"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element if both elements are present. Note that the offset reflects the intended musical position for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change in sound. It should not be used to compensate for latency issues in particular hardware configurations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<sound>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Music","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"],"anchor":"Music"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Group-swift.struct"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/init(id:group:swing:offset:tempo:dynamics:isDaCapo:segno:dalsegno:coda:tocoda:divisions:impliesForwardRepeat:fine:timeOnly:isPizzicato:pan:elevation:damperPedal:softPedal:sostenutoPedal:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/coda","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/dalsegno","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/damperPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/divisions","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/dynamics","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/elevation","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/fine","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/group-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/impliesForwardRepeat","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isDaCapo","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isPizzicato","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/offset","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/pan","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/segno","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/softPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/sostenutoPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/swing","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/tempo","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/timeOnly","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/tocoda"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSoundV","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSound","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLSound","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/softPedal":{"title":"softPedal","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/softpedal","abstract":[{"text":"Controls playback of the soft pedal. A numeric value from 0 to 100 may be used for half pedaling.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"softPedal","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLYesNoNumberO","text":"MXLYesNoNumber","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/softPedal","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMusicItem":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLMusicItem","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for a music item."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMusicItem","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMusicItem","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmusicitem"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDirection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFullNote":{"title":"MXLFullNote","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFullNote"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfullnote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFullNote"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote","abstract":[{"text":"The full-note group is a sequence of the common note elements between cue\/grace notes and regular (full)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notes: pitch, chord, and rest information, but not duration (cue and grace notes do not have duration","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoded). Unpitched elements are used for unpitched percussion, speaking voice, and other musical elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lacking determinate pitch.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/coda":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/coda","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/coda","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"coda"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"coda","abstract":[{"text":"Names a coda sign for a forward jump, used to distinguish between multiple jumps.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/damperPedal":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/damperPedal","abstract":[{"text":"Controls playback of the damper pedal. A numeric value from 0 to 100 may be used for half pedaling.","type":"text"}],"title":"damperPedal","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/damperpedal","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"damperPedal","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLYesNoNumberO","text":"MXLYesNoNumber","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/divisions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/divisions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of divisions per quarter note, used together with the segno or coda attributes."}],"title":"divisions","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/divisions","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"divisions","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/impliesForwardRepeat":{"abstract":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether a forward repeat sign is implied but not displayed.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"impliesForwardRepeat","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/impliesforwardrepeat","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/impliesForwardRepeat","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"impliesForwardRepeat","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/dynamics":{"abstract":[{"text":"The dynamics (or MIDI velocity), expressed as a percentage of the default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"dynamics","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/dynamics","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/dynamics","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dynamics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLNonNegativeDecimala","text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/Equatable-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Equatable-Implementations","abstract":[],"title":"Equatable Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/equatable-implementations","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLAttributes","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","abstract":[{"text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAttributes"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAttributes"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/pan":{"abstract":[{"text":"Deprecated in favor of the pan element in midi-instrument. Specifies placement of sound in a 3-D space","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the listener, in degrees."}],"role":"symbol","title":"pan","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/pan","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/pan","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLRotationDegreesa","text":"MXLRotationDegrees","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch":{"title":"MXLPitch","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pitch is represented as a combination of the step of the diatonic scale, the chromatic alteration, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"octave."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/group-swift.property":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/group-swift.property","title":"group","abstract":[{"text":"The instrument changes, MIDI device and instrument assignments, and playback techniques associated with this","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"sound element, grouped by instrument.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/group-swift.property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"group","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSoundV5GroupV","text":"Group","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/elevation":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/elevation","abstract":[{"text":"Deprecated in favor of the elevation element in midi-instrument. Specifies placement of sound in a 3-D space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the listener, in degrees.","type":"text"}],"title":"elevation","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/elevation","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"elevation","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLRotationDegreesa","text":"MXLRotationDegrees","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/offset":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The offset of the sound from the current score position."}],"role":"symbol","title":"offset","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/offset","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/offset","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"offset"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOffsetV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLOffset"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/isDaCapo":{"type":"topic","title":"isDaCapo","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isDaCapo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to go back to the beginning of the movement."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDaCapo"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/isdacapo"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/id":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/id","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies an id reference."}],"title":"id","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/id","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/isPizzicato":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/isPizzicato","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether following notes are played pizzicato ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":") or arco ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"title":"isPizzicato","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/ispizzicato","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isPizzicato","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/tocoda":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Names the coda sign to jump forward to, used to distinguish between multiple jumps."}],"role":"symbol","title":"tocoda","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/tocoda","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/tocoda","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tocoda","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","title":"Swift.Hashable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLSound","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSound","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSound","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/segno":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/segno","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Names a segno sign for a backward jump, used to distinguish between multiple jumps."}],"title":"segno","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/segno","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segno","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLRest":{"title":"MXLRest","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLRest","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLRest","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlrest","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The rest element indicates notated rests or silences. Rest elements are usually empty, but placement on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"staff can be specified using display-step and display-octave elements. If the measure attribute is set to yes,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this indicates this is a complete measure rest."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/dalsegno":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/dalsegno","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Names the segno sign to jump back to, used to distinguish between multiple jumps."}],"title":"dalsegno","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/dalsegno","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dalsegno","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/timeOnly":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/timeOnly","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times through a repeat this sound element applies to, if only particular times."}],"title":"timeOnly","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/timeonly","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeOnly","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLTimeOnlya","text":"MXLTimeOnly","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNote","abstract":[{"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/tempo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/tempo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tempo, expressed in quarter notes per minute. A value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" indicates the sound-generating program"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should prompt the user when compiling a sound file."}],"title":"tempo","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/tempo","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tempo","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLNonNegativeDecimala","text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","title":"Swift.Copyable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/sostenutoPedal":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/sostenutoPedal","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/sostenutopedal","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sostenutoPedal","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLYesNoNumber","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLYesNoNumberO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"sostenutoPedal","abstract":[{"text":"Controls playback of the sostenuto pedal. A numeric value from 0 to 100 may be used for half pedaling.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/swing":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The swing to apply in playback, so that notes are played swung rather than even.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/swing","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"swing","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSwing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSwingV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"swing","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/swing","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/Group-swift.struct":{"title":"MXLSound.Group","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Group","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Group","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/group-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/Group-swift.struct","abstract":[{"text":"A grouping of instrument changes, MIDI device and instrument assignments, and playback techniques","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated with a single instrument within a sound element.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"abstract":[{"text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inverted).","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLBarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/fine":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound\/fine","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Follows the final note or rest in a movement with a da capo or dal segno direction. If numeric, represents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the actual duration of the final note or rest."}],"title":"fine","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound\/fine","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fine","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound/init(id:group:swing:offset:tempo:dynamics:isDaCapo:segno:dalsegno:coda:tocoda:divisions:impliesForwardRepeat:fine:timeOnly:isPizzicato:pan:elevation:damperPedal:softPedal:sostenutoPedal:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLS